Track 2: Lenz at the Spindle Drift
- Story & Context: Tucked inside the timber-braced alcove known as the Spindle Drift, night-watch mechanic Lenz fought off bone-chilling dampness by running his dented BBb tuba through a battery-powered tape loop while his partner tapped steady rim-shots against an air regulator valve. With grease and coal dust embedded deep beneath his fingernails, Lenz unburdened his chest into a carbon microphone, delivering a syncopated, rhythmic confession about the home he left behind in the sunlight. A burst air hose hissed in perfect syncopation with the Rhodes piano, turning a routine safety hazard into the coziest pocket of warmth in the entire underground basin. "I patch my pride with a ten-gauge thread, but the groove sleeps lighter than the rock overhead," he whispered in a rhythmic old-school cadence, his voice cushioned by the deep brass rumble.
